# #1002 legacy persisted Chat contract (documented before implementation).
# Use only disposable local test data. No additional login/provider is introduced.
# Every persistence operation requires the existing JWT authentication handler AND
# successful MCP GET /api/auth/me with this exact user's bearer and explicit selectors.
# Actor = validated directory tid + oid; selected organization/person/mode comes from /me.
# No caller UserId, role, email, context owner, or default service credential grants access.
# New conversations receive a versioned qualified-owner key; old ownerless rows remain
# inaccessible. Nullable additive columns do NOT adopt/migrate any legacy ownership.
# A conversation can bind a system on its first message/context update only; that
# system is checked at the upstream workspace-access route before history is returned.
# Changing system after history exists is rejected: create another conversation.
# Revoked membership, invalid tokens, /me outage/mismatch fail before Chat DB access.
# Hub join/send/typing use the same checks, not client-provided group authorization.
# Responses/progress are delivered to the invoking connection, not a persistent group:
# a stale previously-joined connection must never receive later private history.
# All service operations honor the trusted HTTP RequestAborted token; channel send
# also exposes explicit cancellation linked to that request lifetime.
# Manual verification: create as A, send twice, GET messages/search/history; replay
# each conversation/message/attachment ID with B, another directory, organization,
# or ordinary/support mode: no content and no writes. Confirm ownerless rows 404.
# Cancel an active request and confirm cancellation reaches upstream/EF operations.
# Deployment: Chat startup adds nullable Conversations.OwnerKey/SystemId columns
# for SQLite/SQL Server; it never backfills either column. Back up the Chat database
# before deployment. Rollback may leave these additive columns in place, but do not
# expose a pre-isolation Chat binary against persisted sensitive history.
@chat = https://localhost:5001
@token = REPLACE_WITH_USER_BEARER
@organization = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@conversation = REPLACE_WITH_CREATED_ID
@message = REPLACE_WITH_CREATED_MESSAGE_ID

### Create (UserId is deliberately forged; it must never select ownership).
POST {{chat}}/api/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Workspace isolation manual test","userId":"forged-owner"}

### First message, then repeat for continuation.
POST {{chat}}/api/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"conversationId":"{{conversation}}","message":"Explain the RMF phases"}

### History (repeat with a different user's token or workspace).
GET {{chat}}/api/messages?conversationId={{conversation}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Search ignores caller-supplied ownership filters.
GET {{chat}}/api/conversations/search?query=Workspace&userId=forged-owner
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Denied without explicit selectors (no implicit home workspace).
GET {{chat}}/api/conversations/{{conversation}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Support is a separate scope; only this mode forwards ato-impersonate.
GET {{chat}}/api/conversations/{{conversation}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: support
Cookie: ato-impersonate=REPLACE_WITH_VALID_SUPPORT_COOKIE

### Delete own disposable conversation only.
DELETE {{chat}}/api/conversations/{{conversation}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
